WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.530
[Caroline] For the past two years,

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.230
I've had the opportunity
to travel with my friends

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.633
to amazing destinations.

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:07.910
While we can't travel this year,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.969
I am virtually meeting
up with them to share

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:11.980
our favorite travel memories,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.541
and where we're looking
forward to heading next.

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:22.500
Oh my gosh, I missed you guys.

00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:27.220
My friends and I have experienced
life-changing adventures

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.960
across the US and Europe, empowered by

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.158
my Marriott Bonvoy Boundless™ Card.

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:34.167
Earlier this year, we began planning for

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.220
"Travel Dares Season 3,"
but as you can expect

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.032
our travels were put on hold.

00:00:39.032 --> 00:00:42.220
If you're watching this video,
you probably had to cancel

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.950
a trip or two yourself.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.606
So, why not let our
adventures on "Travel Dares"

00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:49.008
inspire your future trip planning?

00:00:54.113 --> 00:00:55.240
[Joe] I know what my favorite one was.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.917
It was the extreme tubing
we did in Salt Lake City.

00:00:57.917 --> 00:01:00.350
The view going down that
hill on that inner tube

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.890
was amazing, it was such a rush.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.380
I was talking about that
weeks after that trip.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.427
It was just such a rush,
and it was so much fun.

00:01:07.427 --> 00:01:11.497
[Nico] I have to say it was the
suspension bridge in France.

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:13.830
The feeling of even getting up there,

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.136
we were just like, 'Oh my God,
we're going higher and higher'

00:01:17.136 --> 00:01:19.040
what's going to happen?
And then we get there

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.050
and the bridge is like this wide.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.950
And we're like, we're gonna get on that?

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.330
Definitely that was like
something I would never do

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.870
on my own, but for this
show, I was like, 'OK,

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:31.584
we're doing it,' and I'm glad I did.

00:01:31.584 --> 00:01:33.700
No one can ever say
anything to me ever again.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.090
I am the bravest woman alive,
and I don't care what you say.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.158
[Aj] Alright, so my favorite dare was

00:01:39.158 --> 00:01:41.761
definitely the water slide in Austria.

00:01:41.761 --> 00:01:43.570
I don't know why, but
there's just something

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.170
about being thrown 25 feet
in the air, like a rag doll,

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.668
that I just really love.

00:01:48.668 --> 00:01:51.520
I wanna go back, and do it again so bad.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.839
[Caroline] Maybe I would have

00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:55.120
to say when Joe dared me

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.000
to go in the individual
submarines in The Bahamas.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.360
I love the water, and we got
to be so close to marine life,

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.290
and it's a very safe way
for us and the environment.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.458
And it was just so nice
to just be in the ocean

00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:12.659
and feel the water and everything.

00:02:12.659 --> 00:02:16.130
[Joe] I have to know. I saw
the video, but from you guys,

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.032
I wanna ask you, what was it
like being into quicksand?

00:02:19.032 --> 00:02:21.401
[Aj] I don't know, it's
kinda hard to describe.

00:02:21.401 --> 00:02:22.935
You don't feel it when you're in there.

00:02:22.935 --> 00:02:24.437
But once you try to move,

00:02:24.437 --> 00:02:26.372
that's when it actually pulls on you.

00:02:26.372 --> 00:02:29.170
[Caroline] The way it feels,
it's almost like you're glued

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.140
and cemented into the ground,

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.346
until you start doing the technique of

00:02:33.346 --> 00:02:35.940
kind of wiggling your leg.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.700
It's kind of a strange
feeling, but once you're free,

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.210
you can move and wiggle your legs again,

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.710
which is the first thing I did.

00:02:48.728 --> 00:02:50.860
[Joe] The Bahamas.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.510
I had never been to any
sort of tropical island

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.390
or tropical destination in my
life - this was my first time.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.238
And everything about
that trip was amazing.

00:02:59.238 --> 00:03:02.190
The second I stepped off the
plane, I was just like,'wow!'

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.830
I mean, I loved the
food, I loved the people,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.030
I loved how everything
looked, I loved the beach.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.590
I loved the hotel we stayed
at, The Coral At Atlantis.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:11.720
Everything about that from start
to finish, I was just like,

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.687
'yes, I understand why
people vacation here.'

00:03:14.687 --> 00:03:17.890
[Aj] For me, it was definitely Naples.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.580
Mostly because it's a coastal city,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.470
there's water everywhere.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.099
We were taking boats to places
and I really loved that.

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:28.780
Everything about Naples
was what I want

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.336
in a vacation spot.

00:03:30.336 --> 00:03:32.510
[Nico] Every time people ask
me what my favorite place was,

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.473
I say Switzerland.

00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:36.310
Because I've never breathed

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.970
as fresh air as I did there .

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.400
It was so weird, I was like,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.310
why does everything feel so good here?

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.340
Everything's just so beautiful,
natural, skies were blue.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.621
It was perfect, out of a storybook.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.896
Aside from learning, how
popular and delicious

00:03:56.896 --> 00:04:00.087
the khachapuri was, I think
the fact that there are

00:04:00.087 --> 00:04:04.010
40 variations of it was
kind of mind blowing.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.720
And now I guess we have
to go back to Georgia

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.060
and try the others.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.020
Oh my God that is so good.

00:04:11.043 --> 00:04:13.570
[Caroline] For me, when we
went to Wales, and we went on

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:16.770
the Pontcysyllte Aqueduct,
it was really cool

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.960
because it not only was
a stunning structure

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.387
and a world heritage site,

00:04:21.387 --> 00:04:23.300
but it was something that was built,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.890
in the early 1800s

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.894
So the engineering, is just incredible.

00:04:31.597 --> 00:04:35.130
[Nico] The Renaissance
Aix-en-Provence was probably

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.804
the coolest hotel I had ever seen.

00:04:37.804 --> 00:04:41.250
There was this one room we
went to, and it had all of this

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.660
really, really cool local art,

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.150
and some of it was interactive.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.013
I had never seen anything like it.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.770
[Joe] I'm going to be
going to Rome, Italy.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.120
My wife has never been to
Italy, and I used to live there.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.180
So, we are still planning to go there,

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.058
the first chance we get.

00:04:59.058 --> 00:05:03.220
[Aj] So, Paris is on the
list as the next trip now.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.180
So going back to Paris, and
I'm actually really excited

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.060
about that because I had
a great time in Paris.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.480
[Nico] So I'm actually half Dominican,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.270
and I've never been to
the Dominican Republic.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.260
It's always been one of those places that,

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.820
I really wanted to go.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:21.610
It's white sand beaches,
crystal-clear blue water.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.150
It's gorgeous. There's so much greenery.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.130
And I'm gonna get to
meet a bunch of family

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.830
that I've never met
before in my entire life.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.230
So, I feel like something
like that would be

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.495
a dream vacation once I
can do it. Hopefully soon.

00:05:35.495 --> 00:05:37.840
[Caroline] So the first
place I'd love to travel to,

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.220
when we're able to do so is,
I want to go back to Armenia

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.500
with my family because I'm
Armenian and I went there

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.220
last year for a short
period of time for work.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.700
And, it was amazing
because I was able to meet

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.880
so many family members
I've never met before,

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.081
and just learn about the
country's history and heritage.

00:05:55.081 --> 00:05:57.850
I also want to take my mom back to Armenia

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.570
and have her see it after so
many years of not being there,

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.100
and just see how the
country's changed and stuff.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.740
So, I'm trying to save up a lot of points

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.027
to make that trip happen for us.

00:06:08.027 --> 00:06:11.340
[Aj] I've never traveled
abroad until Travel Dares.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:15.601
So this is my first experience,
leaving the country.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:18.030
You really see how big the world is,

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:20.273
and how much there is to experience.

00:06:20.273 --> 00:06:22.700
I just see the world just
completely different now.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.078
And I'm just so grateful to
have had that opportunity.

00:06:26.078 --> 00:06:28.260
[Joe] Thanks to Travel
Dares, I got to travel to

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.490
parts of this country
that I probably don't know

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.960
if I would have ever gone before,
especially Salt Lake City.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.723
I was like, 'whoa, this city
rules.' Utah is incredible.

00:06:37.723 --> 00:06:41.290
And Santa Fe, New Mexico
is another place that

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.970
just never was really on my radar.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.080
The show really gave me an opportunity,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.910
to see parts of this country
that I hadn't seen before.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.540
And I'm very glad that I did because now

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.103
I really want to explore
more of the United States.

00:06:51.103 --> 00:06:56.100
[Nico] For me, I've kind of
always been a little bit scared,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.178
of the unexpected, of the new.

00:06:59.178 --> 00:07:01.780
But, this whole experience has

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.650
completely changed my mind.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.740
Now I want more of the new.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.400
I want more of the things
that I've never done before,

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.424
never seen before, never eaten before.

00:07:11.424 --> 00:07:14.390
And now I feel like I'm
welcoming the new experiences,

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.095
instead of being scared of them.

00:07:16.095 --> 00:07:19.932
[Caroline] I can't wait to
travel with you all so soon.

00:07:19.932 --> 00:07:20.863
Where are we going to go?

00:07:20.863 --> 00:07:22.101
We should plan it now.

00:07:22.101 --> 00:07:23.669
[Nico] That's what we have
to start thinking about.

00:07:23.669 --> 00:07:26.906
Where are we going next,
on our next adventure?

00:07:26.906 --> 00:07:28.460
[Caroline] And we hope our past adventures

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.560
inspire you to make
future trip plans, too.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.280
So that you're ready to go when
we're able to explore again.

